{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation evidence, measured in `.rebar/worktrees/impl-25a4` at base `778c969e4f1`.\n\n## Deviation: AC8 cannot be met as written — the diff is 6 paths, not 5\n\nAC8 and AC9 are in direct conflict. Deleting `for legacy in _LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES: sig.append((legacy, os.environ.get(legacy)))` from `_env_signature` removes an `os.environ.get(<non-literal>)` call site that the **generated** `docs/env-vars.md` enumerates by file and line. `make lint` runs `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`, which then fails:\n\n```\ndocs/env-vars.md is stale — regenerate with `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py`\nmake: *** [lint] Error 1\n```\n\n`make verify` begins with `make lint`, so AC9 is unreachable while AC8's 5-path diff holds. I regenerated the file. The regeneration is purely mechanical and entirely attributable to this change — one removed entry plus line-number drift in the same block, nothing else in the 169-section document moved:\n\n```\n-- `src/rebar/config.py:284` ... :297 ... :301 ... :308 ... :565\n+- `src/rebar/config.py:282` ... :295 ... :302 ... :559\n```\n\n`:301` was the deleted `os.environ.get(legacy)` line itself; the other 4 are the same 4 call sites renumbered by the 12 removed lines. 5 entries → 4.\n\n**The final diff is 6 paths**: the 5 AC8 names plus `docs/env-vars.md`. This is the same latent-AC defect class already recorded on `dc42-...`, `db2c-3a4b-1826-451f`, and `a018-a2c0-fc15-434c` — an AC whose own command can never pass as written. Fifth confirmed member.\n\n## Second deviation: one stale comment beyond the 4 enumerated edits\n\n`_env_signature`'s docstring read \"Hash discovery pointers, overrides, **aliases**, and tombstones for cache keys.\" The aliases pass is gone, so the docstring named a contributor that no longer exists. Reworded to \"Hash discovery pointers, canonical overrides, and tombstones for cache keys.\" Same file as step 3, inside the function the step deletes from; no behavior change.\n\n## AC results\n\n| AC | Result |\n|---|---|\n| AC1 `git grep _LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` | ✓ exit 1, no output |\n| AC2 `git grep _map_legacy_env` | ✓ exit 1, no output |\n| AC3 import both modules | ✓ exit 0 |\n| AC4 3 named test modules | ✓ 32 passed in 32.08s |\n| AC5 cache-invalidation test | ✓ added, passes |\n| AC6 `ruff check src tests` | ✓ \"All checks passed!\" |\n| AC7 `make typecheck` | ✓ 747 source files, no issues |\n| AC8 exactly 5 paths | ✗ **6** — see deviation above |\n| AC9 `make verify` | queued (serial; 19ba holds the host) |\n\n`make lint` in full (not just `ruff`) also passes, covering the module-size, complexity, mechanism-delta, config-ownership, config-read, zizmor and actionlint gates.\n\n## AC5 — what the new test actually pins\n\nAdded `test_canonical_env_change_mid_process_invalidates_the_config_cache` to `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`. It drives 3 transitions against a tmp repo root, each of which must flip the resolved value, so each proves a distinct cache miss:\n\n1. unset → `suggest_duplicate_tickets is False` (default)\n2. `REBAR_VERIFY_SUGGEST_DUPLICATE_TICKETS=1` → `is True`\n3. `delenv` → `is False`\n\nSteps 2 and 3 are the set and the unset the Testing section asked for. This is the test that makes the deletion safe: it demonstrates the canonical pass is what invalidates, so removing a pass over a permanently-empty dict changes nothing observable.\n\n## AC4 — confirming it passed for the right reason\n\nThe plan asked that `test_config_surface_golden.py`'s `accounted` set be unchanged in size after dropping the `| set(_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES)` term. It is: `set({})` is the empty set, so the union was already a no-op. `_orphaned_env_vars` returns `[]` both before and after, and `test_live_env_var_gap_is_detected_even_when_removals_are_accounted_for` — which asserts `_orphaned_env_vars(data) == []` on a doctored golden — still passes, so the census still accounts for every pinned env var.\n\nNothing committed or pushed yet."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793397671990586028,"uuid":"0e35243b-8367-457c-b198-b9292bab849f"}